## ⏱️ Step 4: The Core Technical SEO Checklist
To ensure Google indexes and ranks all 100+ pages perfectly, you must pass Google's strict Core Web Vitals parameters:

* Instant Load (Zero Framework Bloat): Do not build these tools using heavy React or Angular frameworks unless necessary. Use plain HTML, CSS, and Vanilla JavaScript. Your total page size should be under 50KB.
* Global Edge Hosting: Host your entire site on a Global Content Delivery Network (CDN) like Vercel, Netlify, or Cloudflare Pages. This duplicates your website files onto servers all over the globe, meaning your tools will load in less than 0.5 seconds whether a user is in London, Tokyo, or New York.
* The Structured Data Layer: For every calculator or FAQ block on your pages, wrap the text in JSON-LD Schema Markup. This tells Google's web crawlers exactly what the page calculates, allowing Google to display interactive widgets or FAQ dropdown elements directly inside the search engine results pages.

